$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Palladium-Catalyzed
Heck Coupling of Pyridyl-Substituted Vinylsilane and Aryl Iodide. To a
solution of Pd2(dba)3•CHCl3 (2.6 mg, 0.0025 rnmol, 0.5 mol %) and
tri-2-furylpbosphine (2.3 mg, 0.01 mmol, 2 mol %) in THF (1.5 mL) were
added iodobenzene (112 mg, 0.55 mmol), 2-pyridyldimethyl(vinyl)silane (1)
(82 mg, 0.50 mmol), and triethylamine (61 mg, 0.60 mmol) at room
temperature under argon and the reaction mixture was stirred at 50°C for
24 h. After cooling to room temperature, toluene (5 mL) was added to the
reaction mixture. This mixture was extracted with 1 N aq HCl (6 x 10 mL).
The combined aqueous phase was neutralized by adding NaHCO3 and then was
extracted with EtOAc (3 x 30 mL). Drying over Na2SO4 and removal of the
solvents under reduced pressure.
(E,E)-2-Pyridyldimethyl(1,3-octadienyl)silane (2h). Yield 90% 1H NMR (300
MHz) δ 0.40 (s, 6 H), 0.88 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3 H), 1.24-1.44 (m, 4 H),
2.04-2.13 (m, 2 H), 5.77 (dt, J= 15.0, 6.9 Hz, 1 H), 5.87 (d, J = 18.6
Hz, 1 H), 6.11 (dd, J = 15.0, 9.9 Hz, 1 H), 6.62 (dd, J = 18.6, 9.9 Hz, 1
H), 7.17 (ddd, J = 7.5,4.8, 1.8 Hz, 1 H), 7.50 (ddd, J = 7.5, 1.8,0.9 Hz,
1 H), 7.56 (td, J= 7.5, 1.8 Hz, 1 H), 8.77 (ddd, J= 4.8, i.8, 0.9 Hz, 1
H); 13C NMR (75 MHz) δ -3.2, 13.9, 22.2, 31.2, 32.2, 122.7, 127.2, 129.4,
133.1, 133.9, 136.9, .146.7, 150.2, 167.2. IR (neat) 1644, 1576, 1451,
1418, 1246 CIJl-I. HRMS (EI) m/z calcd for C15H23NSi: 245.1600, found
245.1603.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
