$DATUM 120-94-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure: To a 25 mL three-neck round bottom flask with a stir
bar was added Pd(TFA)2 (33 mg, 0.1 mmol), neocuproine (42 mg, 0.2 mmol),
LiTFA (24 mg, 0.2 mmol) and NMP (1.5 mL). The flask was evacuated briefly
under vacuum, filled with oxygen gas and sealed with a septum. A balloon
was filled with O2 and connected to an 6-inch needle. The needle attached
to the O2 balloon was inserted through the septum, and the solution was
sparged with O2 gas for ca. 10 min. A solution of (E)- styrenylboronic
acid (222 mg, 1.5 mmol) and allylbenzene (132 μ L, 1 mmol) in NMP (1 mL)
was added. The reaction was heated for 3 h at 40 °C using an oil bath
with vigorous stirring under an O2 atmosphere supplied by the balloon.
Pure product was isolated by using the same procedure described above.
The product yield obtained from the reaction in a round-bottom flask (74%
for 1 mmol scale in 3 hours and 64% for 10 mmol scale in 6 hours) is
lower than that observed using vortexing agitation (88%) partly owing to
the poorer gas-liquid mixing that takes place in the former reaction.
(E)-(3-methylenenon-1-en-1-yl)benzene 3a6. Yield 83%. 6 h, 20:1
regioselectivity. .H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.44-7.19 (m, 5H), 6.81 (d, J
= 16.4 Hz, 1H), 6.58 (d, J = 16.3 Hz, 1H), 5.13 (s, 1H), 5.06 (s, 1H),
2.32 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 1.58-1.50 (m, 2H), 1.42-1.32 (m, 6H), 0.93-0.88
(m, 3H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 146.6, 137.7, 131.4, 128.8, 128.1,
127.6, 126.6, 116.3, 32.3, 32.0, 29.5, 28.5, 22.9, 14.3. HRMS (EI) Calcd.
for C16H22 ([M]+): 214.1717, found: 214.1715.
