$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM ii) Procedures for the synthesis of product 2. 0.3 mmol (1 equiv) of
N-vinylacetamide 1, 0.03 mmol (10 mol%, 6.8 mg) palladium (II)acetate and
0.06 mmol (20 mol%, 15.8 mg) of triphenylphosphine were dissolved in 5 mL
of DMF in a screw cap vial under argon atmosphere. Then 0.6 mmol (60.7
mg, 2.0 equiv) triethylamine was added to the solution and the vial was
heated at 120 °C till the starting material consumed completely. The
solution was cooled to room temperature and diluted with ethyl acetate,
washed with saturated ammonium chloride solution and brine. The organic
layer was dried with anhydrous NaSO4 and filtered. The final filtrate was
concentrated under vacuum to afford the crude product which was isolated
through flash column chromatography (Eluent: petrol ether/ethyl acetate)
to furnish the related product 2. N-(2-(1-phenylvinyl)benzyl)acetamide 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.37-7.10 (m, 9H), 5.73 (s, 1H), 5.22 (s, 1H),
5.17 (s, 1H), 4.11 (d, J = 5.7 Hz, 2H), 1.66 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 169.57, 148.46, 141.36, 140.77, 136.05, 130.41, 129.44, 128.59,
128.18, 128.09, 127.63, 126.60, 115.70, 41.63, 23.04. HRMS (ESI): m/z
calculated for C17H18NO [M+H]+:252.1388 found: 252.1389.
