$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Asymmetric
Palladacyclization of Aryl Triflates (GP1). A base-washed, oven-dried
sealed tube equipped with a magnetic stirring bar and a Teflon® seal was
charged with the appropriate aryl triflate (1 equiv), Pd(OAc)2 (1 equiv)
and the appropriate chiral bisphosphine (2 equiv). Deoxygenated
N,N-dimethylacetamide (DMA, distilled from CaH2 into a sealed tube under
reduced pressure, backfilled with Ar, then sparged with Ar for 2 h, 0.1
M) and 1,2,2,6,6-pentamethylpiperidine (PMP, distilled from CaH2 under
into a sealed tube under reduced pressure, 4 equiv) were added to the
solids. A stream of Ar was bubbled through the resulting mixture for 15
min and then the sealed tube was flushed with a steady stream of Ar for
an additional 15 min. The Teflon® seal was tightened and the solution was
maintained at 70-80 °C until the aryl triflate was no longer detected by
TLC analysis (typically 10-16 h). The solution was allowed to cool to
room temperature, diluted with EtOAc and poured into saturated aqueous
NaHCO3. The aqueous phase was separated and extracted with EtOAc. The
combined organic extracts were dried (Na2SO4) and concentrated onto
silica gel. The residue was immediately purified by flash chromatography
eluting with diethyl ether-hexanes mixtures.Palladacyclization of 2 with
Stoichiometric Pd(0)·( R)-BINAP. Following GP1, a solution of aryl
triflate 2 (50 mg, 85 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (19 mg, 85 mmol), (R)-BINAP (106
mg, 170 mmol), PMP (53 mg, 340 mmol) and DMA (0.9 mL) was maintained at
80 °C for 14 h. After the usual workup, the residue was purified by flash
chromatography (50% diethyl ether-hexanes) to pure samples of 3β and 3α
(94 mg total, 81 mmol, 95%, 96:4 epimeric ratio) as bright yellow
powders: (S ,S )-BDPP Palladacycle (ent -10β). Following GP1, a solution
of aryl triflate 2 (25 mg, 42 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (9.4 mg, 42 mmol), PMP (26
mg, 170 mmol) and DMA (0.5 mL) were maintained at 70 °C for 16 h. After
the usual workup, the residue was purified by flash chromatography (50%
diethyl ether-hexanes) to afford ent -10β (36 mg, 37 mmol, 89%) of as a
colorless solid mp >170 °C, decomposition (Et2O-hexanes); 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.18 (br m, 2H, ArH), 7.77 (t, J= 8.8 Hz, 2H, ArH), 7.59
(t, J= 8.9 Hz, 2H, ArH), 7.39 (d, J= 7.4 Hz, 2H, ArH), 7.31-7.12 (m, 12H,
ArH), 7.02-6.89 (m, 6H, ArH), 6.77-6.74 (m, 3H, ArH), 6.67 (d, J= 7.8 Hz,
1H, ArH), 6.49 (t, J= 7.6 Hz, 1H, ArH), 6.27 (d, J= 7.9 Hz, 1H, ArH),
5.27 (d, J= 15.3 Hz, 1H, CH2), 4.62 (d, J= 15.3 Hz, 1H, CH2),4.20-4.16
(m, 1H, CH2), 3.90 (dd, J= 13.8, 6.9 Hz, 1H, CH2), 3.71-3.67 (M, 1H,
CH2), 3.51 (dd, J= 13.8, 7.3, 1H, CH2), 2.82-2.72 (m, 1H, CH), 2.71-2.61
(m, 1H, CH), 2.00-1.81 (m, 2H, CH2), 1.59-1.51 (m, 4H, CH3, CH), 1.07
(ddd, J= 10.5, 6.9, 3.8 Hz, 3H, CH3), 0.94 (dd, J= 10.7, 7.2 Hz, 3H,
CH3); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 180.54 (dd, 3J(C,P) = 2.4, 0.5 Hz),
180.32 (d, 4J(C,P) = 1.8 Hz), 152.84, 142.36, 136.69, 136.62 (2C),
136.52, 135.05, 134.94, 134.30, 134.05, 132.08, 131.99, 131.70, 131.64,
131.23, 130.87, 130.45, 130.22 (m, 3C), 128.89-127.76 (m, 14C), 126.72,
124.82, 124.03, 122.24, 121.66, 119.15, 108.26, 104.25, 104.21, 65.19,
64.38, 59.73, 44.23, 42.30 (dd, 2J(C,P) = 95.3, 6.3 Hz), 35.97(br), 29.29
(dd, J(C,P) = 19.9, 1.4 Hz), 25.84 (dd, J(C,P) = 23.1, 3.2 Hz), 20.15
(dd, 3J(C,P) = 7.9, 1.0 Hz), 18.62 (dd, J(C,P) = 4.2, 2.3 Hz), 15.66 (d,
J(C,P) = 8.8 Hz); 31P NMR (162 MHz, CDCl3) δ 28.50 (d, 2J(P,P) = 58.5 Hz,
1.00P), 9.31 (d, 2J(P,P) = 58.4 Hz, 0.92P); [α]589 = +176, [α]577 = +187,
[α]546 = +217, [α]435 = +431, [α]405 = +583 (c = 0.21 in CHCl3); IR (thin
film) 2922, 2953, 1691, 1652, 1594, 1463, 1436, 1378, 1231, 1185, 1100,
1054, 1019, 980, 942, 799, 753, 722, 699 cm-1; LRMS (ESI+) Calcd for
C56H53N2O4P2Pd (M+H)+: 985.25. Found: 985.27.
