$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Cross-coupling of 4-iodoacetophenone with (Z)-tri(ethoxy)(vinyl-d
2)silane (Scheme 10). (Z)-tri(ethoxy)(vinyl-d 2)silane (0.054 mL, 0.24
mmol), NaOH (49.0 mg, 0.4 mmol) and THF (2mL) were sequentially added to
an oven-dried, 25-mL Schlenk tube equipped with a magnetic stir bar,
septum and argon inlet. The mixture was stirred for 3 h at room
temperature prior to the addition of 4-iodoacetophenone (50.2 mg, 0.20
mmol) and [Pd(OAc)2] (1.1 mg, 5.0 μmol). The solution was heated to 60 °C
for 30 min, then the crude reaction mixture was extracted with ethyl
acetate (20 mL) and washed with water (3 × 5 mL). The ethyl acetate
solution was dried over MgSO4 and evaporated to dryness under vacuum. The
styrene derivative was obtained as a colorless oil after purification by
chromatography with hexane/ethyl acetate 6:1 (R f = 0.30) on a silica gel
column. The distribution of deuterated derivatives was analyzed by 1H NMR
spectroscopy (Figure S7). The samples of (Z)-triethoxy(vinyl-d 2)silane
((Z)-33-d 2) were contaminated with a 7% of the (E) isotopomer.
Therefore, the selectivity of the transformation of (Z)-33-d 2 into
(Z)-31-d 2 can be estimated to be greater than 96%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, Hiyama reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Mechanistic Studies on the Pd-Catalyzed Vinylation of Aryl Halides with
Vinylalkoxysilanes in Water: The Effect of the Solvent and NaOH Promoter
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Gordillo, Alvaro; Ortuno, Manuel A.; Lopez-Mardomingo, Carmen; Lledos,
Agusti; Ujaque, Gregori; de Jesus, Ernesto
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2013), 135(37), 13749-13763

