$DATUM 127-19-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The Heck reaction of aryl bromides with styrene in the presence of
catalysts 5a and 5b (Table 1). General Procedure: An oven-dried Schlenk
flask was charged under argon with bromobenzene (527 μL, 784 mg 5.0
mmol), styrene (690 μL, 648 mg, 6.0 mmol), anhydrous KOAc (589 mg, 6.0
mmol) and DMA (5.0 mL). A solution of catalyst 5a in DMA (4.48 x 10-4 M,
90 μL, 8.0 x 10-4 mol %) was then added via syringe. The flask was sealed
and placed in a 140 oC oil bath controlled by a J-KEMP temperature
controller and stirred for 24 h. After cooling to rt, the reaction
mixture was poured into water (200 mL) and extracted with EtOAc (3 x 50
mL). The combined organic extracts were washed with brine, dried with
anhydrous Na2SO4, and concentrated. Purification by flash chromatography
on silica gel (hexanes/CH2Cl2 1:1) gave trans-stilbene along with a trace
amount of its regioisomer (790 mg, 87%). trans-Stilbene2-5 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.66 (d, 4 H, J = 7.8 Hz), 7.51 (t, 4 H, J = 7.6 Hz), 7.41
(t, 2 H, J = 7.3 Hz), 7.27 (s, 2 H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ 137.51,
128.88, 128.84, 127.77, 126.70.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective, Heck reaction, other product also
detected
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Carbocyclic Carbene Ligands Derived from Aromatic Nitrones: Formation and
Catalytic Activity of Their Pd(II) Complexes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Yao, Qingwei; Zabawa, Mark; Woo, Joyce; Zheng, Chong
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2007), 129(11), 3088-3089

