$DATUM 2-(2-Vinylphenyl)-1,2-dideuteroethanol. The title compound was prepared
according to a general procedure for Stille cross-couplings.4 The alcohol
from the previous step (800 mg, 3.94 mmol, 1.00 equiv), tributylvinyltin
(1.31 g, 4.13 mmol, 1.05 equiv), Pd2dba3 (36 mg, 0.039 mmol, 0.010
equiv), and P(t-Bu)3 (17.5 mg, 0.084 mmol, 0.020 equiv) were stirred in
toluene (4 mL) under argon for 24 h. Then, KF (3 g) was added, followed
by Et2O (10 mL) and activated carbon (3 g). The mixture was stirred for 5
min, and then it was filtered through a pad of silica (washed with Et2O
(3 x 20 mL)). The filtrate was concentrated, and the residue was purified
by column chromatography (5:1 hexanes:EtOAc), which furnished 520 mg of
the desired product. 2-(2-Vinylphenyl)-1,2-dideuteroethanol, yield 88% 1H
NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ 7.57-7.49 (m, 1H), 7.31-7.18 (m, 3H), 7.02 (dd, J
= 17.4 Hz, 11.0 Hz, 1H), 5.66 (dd, J = 17.3 Hz, 1.4 Hz, 1H), 5.32 (dd, J
= 11.0 Hz, 1.4 Hz, 1H), 3.79 (t, J = 6.6 Hz, 1H), 2.95 (d, J = 7.0 Hz,
1H), 1.44 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz) δ 137.3, 135.9,
134.6, 130.6, 128.1, 127.2, 126.3, 116.3, 63.0 (t, J = 21.9 Hz), 36.2 (t,
J = 19.5 Hz); IR (film) 3346, 3087, 3063, 3027, 2922, 2166, 1834, 1626,
1484, 1450, 1416, 1332, 1098, 1024, 991, 914, 772 cm-1; GCMS (EI) calcd
for C10H10D2O 150 [M]+, found 150.
