$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(R,E,E)-4-Benzylidene-2-(3-phenyl-2-propenyl)-1,2,3,4-tetrahydro-2-naphthalenol
[(R,E,E)-13]- typical procedure for desymmetrizing Heck cyclizations: At
room temperature, a sealed tube was charged with Pd(OAc)2 (4.5 mg, 0.020
mmol, 5.0 mol%), (R)-BINAP (0.019 g, 0.030 mmol, 7.5 mol%) and K2CO3
(0.220 g, 1.59 mmol) under a static pressure of argon. A solution of
triflate (E,E)-9 (0.200 g, 0.398 mmol) and degassed dry toluene (5.5 mL)
was added and the tube was sealed. The resulting suspension was
vigorously stirred for 1 h until the formation of a red homogenous
solution except for the solid base and then heated at 60°C for 36 h. At
room temperature, a small amount of silica gel was added and after
evaporation of the solvents, the crude product on silical gel was
directly purified by flash column chromatography on silica gel
(cyclohexane/t-butyl methyl ether 9:1) giving (R,E,E)-13 (0.115 g, 82%)
as a colorless oil. The enantiomeric excess was determined by HPLC
analysis (94% ee). As determined from the 1H NMR spectra, (R,E,E)-13 was
isomerically pure.
(R*,E,E)-3-Benzylidene-1-(3-phenyl-2-propenyl)-1-indanol [(R*,E,E)-17]:
According to the procedure described for (R,E,E)-13, Heck reaction of
(E,E)-8 (0.101 g, 0.207 mmol) with Pd(OAc)2 (2.3 mg, 0.010 mmol, 5.0
mol%), (R)-BINAP (9.6 mg, 0.015 mmol, 7.5 mol%) and 2,2,6,6-
tetramethylpiperidine (0.141 mL, 0.117 g, 0.825 mmol) in toluene (2.7 mL)
at 80°C for 15 h gave after purification by flash column chromatography
on silica gel (cyclohexane/t-butyl methyl ether 9:1) (R*,E,E)-17 (0.061
g, 87%) as a colorless oil. The enantiomeric excess was determined by
HPLC analysis (26% ee). As determined from the 1H NMR spectra,
(R*,E,E)-17 was isomerically pure. R f=0.30 (cyclohexane/t-butyl methyl
ether 3:1); HPLC (Daicel Chiracel AD, n-heptane/i-PrOH 9:1, flowrate= 1
mL/min, λ=295 nm): t R=15.59 (major), t R=22.61 (minor); [α]D 20=-12.6
(c=0.198, CHCl3, 26% ee); 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ=7.63 (dd, J=6.9, 0.4
Hz, 1 H), 7.44-7.48 (m, 3 H), 7.35-7.41 (m, 4 H), 7.31-7.35 (m, 3 H),
7.27-7.31 (m, 2 H), 7.23 (tt, J=7.1, 1.8 Hz, 1 H), 7.04 (dd, J=2.4, 2.4
Hz, 1 H), 6.52 (d, J=15.8 Hz, 1 H), 6.29 (ddd, J=15.8, 7.4, 7.4 Hz, 1 H),
3.42 (dd, J=16.9, 2.1 Hz, 1 H), 3.18 (dd, J=16.9, 2.5 Hz, 1 H), 2.83
(ddd, J=13.9, 7.6, 1.0 Hz, 1 H), 2.73 (ddd, J=13.9, 7.1, 1.3 Hz, 1 H),
2.29 (s, 1 H) ppm; 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ=148.1, 141.5, 139.0,
137.7, 137.3, 134.2, 129.0, 128.8, 128.7, 128.6, 128.6, 127.4, 126.8,
126.3, 124.9, 123.6, 120.8, 120.3, 81.6, 46.5, 45.2 ppm; IR (CHCl3):
ν=3680, 3590, 3021, 1947, 1802, 1647, 1597, 1493, 1423, 1223, 1023, 924,
799 cm-1; MS (CI-NH3): m/z (%): 354 (2) [(M+NH4)+], 321 (100) [(M-OH)+];
HRMS (EI): m/z calcd for C27H20 [(M-H2O)+]: 320.15652; found: 320.15650.
