$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure. The synthesis of 18 is given as reference. In a 35 mL
pressure tube, triethoxyvinylsilane (0.77 mL, 3.5 mmol) was added to an
aqueous sodium hydroxide 0.50 M solution (10.7 mL, 5.35 mmol) containing
a 20% (w/w) of PEG 2000 (2.14 g). The mixture was vigorously stirred for
5 min at room temperature and 3-bromopyridine (0.178 mL, 1.78 mmol) and
palladium(II) acetate (0.4 mg, 1.8 μmol) were subsequently added. The
reaction mixture was vigorously stirred for 3 h at 140 °C. Then,
1-(4-bromophenyl)ethanone (0.3615 g, 1.80 mmol) and palladium(II) acetate
(0.4 mg, 1.8 μmol) were added and the reaction mixture was again stirred
for 6 h at 140 °C. When the reaction time elapsed, the mixture was worked
up as described above. (E)-1-(4-acetylphenyl)-2-(3-pyridyl)ethene (18).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, thermal, Heck reaction, sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Mechanistic Studies on the Pd-Catalyzed Vinylation of Aryl Halides with
Vinylalkoxysilanes in Water: The Effect of the Solvent and NaOH Promoter
