$DATUM General procedure for the 1,4-palladium alkyl to aryl migration. A
mixture of aryl halide (0.25 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (2.8 mg, 0.0125 mmol),
bis(diphenylphosphino)methane (4.8 mg, 0.0125 mmol), cesium pivalate
(0.1170 g, 0.5 mmol), and the indicated amounts of alkene (if employed)
in dry DMF (4 mL) was quickly flushed with argon and stirred at the
indicated reaction temperature. The reaction was monitored by TLC and gas
chromatographic analysis. After the reaction was complete, it was diluted
with ethyl ether, washed with satd aq NaHCO3, dried over Na2SO4,
concentrated, and purified by flash chromatography on silica gel.
10b-Methyl-1,10b-dihydro-2H-indeno[1,2,3-de]chromene (2). The reaction
mixture was chromatographed using 40:1 hexane/EtOAc to afford 49 mg of
the indicated compound (88 % yield) as a white solid. mp 51-53 °C; 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ 1.46 (s, 3H), 1.63-1.70 (ddd, J = 8.0, 11.2, 11.2 Hz, 1H),
2.29-2.33 (ddd, J = 0.8, 8.0, 11.2 Hz, 1H), 4.56 (ddd, J = 0.8, 8.0, 13.2
Hz, 1H), 4.65 (ddd, J = 8.0, 11.2, 13.2 Hz, 1H), 6.71-6.75 (m, 1H),
7.22-7.26 (m, 2H), 7.29 (dd, J = 1.2, 7.2 Hz, 1H), 7.33-7.37 (m, 1H),
7.42-7.44 (m, 1H), 7.69-7.72 (m, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 25.7, 31.0, 42.6,
65.7, 112.5, 113.8, 121.3, 123.2, 127.1, 127.5, 129.5, 134.9, 140.4,
140.6, 153.0, 153.9; IR (CHCl3, cm-1) 3053, 3010, 2963, 2919, 1614, 1592,
1486, 1447; HRMS Calcd for C16H14O: 222.1045. Found: 222.1048.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Pd-Catalyzed Alkyl to Aryl Migration and Cyclization: An Efficient
Synthesis of Fused Polycycles via Multiple C-H Activation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
