$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(R,E,E)-1-Benzylidene-3-methoxy-3-(3-phenyl-2-propenyl)-1,2,3,4-tetrahydronaphthalene
[(R,E,E)-15]: According to the procedure described for (R,E,E)-13, Heck
reaction of (E,E)-11 (0.230 g, 0.445 mmol) with Pd(OAc)2 (5.0 mg, 0.022
mmol, 5.0 mol%), (R)-BINAP (0.021 g, 0.033 mmol, 7.5 mol%) and degassed
2,2,6,6-tetramethylpiperidine (0.300 mL, 0.249 g, 1.76 mmol) in toluene
(4.5 mL) at 50°C for 36 h afforded after purification by flash column
chromatography on silica gel (cyclohexane/t-butyl methyl ether 98:2)
desired (R,E,E)-15 (0.160 g, 98%) as a colorless oil. The enantiomeric
excess was determined by HPLC analysis (97% ee). As determined from the
1H NMR spectra, (R,E,E)-15 was isomerically pure.
(R,E,E)-1-Benzylidene-3-methoxy-3-(3-phenyl-2-propenyl)-1,2,3,4-tetrahydronaphthalene
R f=0.55 (cyclohexane/t-butyl methyl ether 9:1); HPLC (Daicel Chiracel
AD-H, n-heptane/i-PrOH 95:5, flow rate=1 mL/min, λ=295 nm): t R=9.21 min
(S), t R=10.17 min (R); [α]D 20=-60.9 (c=0.960, CHCl3, 97% ee); 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ=7.74-7.77 (m, 1 H), 7.33-7.40 (m, 4 H), 7.17-7.29 (m,
9 H), 7.14-7.16 (m, 1 H), 6.34 (d, J=15.9 Hz, 1 H), 6.13 (ddd, J=15.8,
7.7, 6.8 Hz, 1 H), 3.18 (s, 3 H), 3.06 (d, J=16.3 Hz, 1 H), 3.00 (m, 2
H), 2.90 (d, J=14.5 Hz, 1 H), 2.48 (ddd, J=14.3, 6.5, 1.4 Hz, 1 H), 2.41
(ddd, J=14.7, 7.8, 1.2 Hz, 1 H) ppm; 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ=137.9,
137.5, 135.3, 135.0, 134.8, 133.0, 129.8, 129.4, 128.4, 128.3, 127.9,
127.1, 126.7, 126.4, 126.2, 125.8, 125.2, 124.0, 76.2, 49.2, 39.9, 38.5,
35.9 ppm; IR (CHCl3): ν=3694, 3027, 2930, 2831, 1950, 1600, 1495, 1455,
1197, 1088, 969 cm-1; MS (CI-NH3): m/z (%): 384 (70) [(M+NH4)+];
elemental analysis calcd (%) for C27H26O: C 88.48, H 7.15; found: C
88.33, H 7.31.
