$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical experiment for the Heck reaction A 10 mL resealable Schlenk flask
containing 0.5 mL of the ionic liquid solution prepared above (0.001 mmol
of palladium based on the initial quantity of palladacycle used) charged
with diisopropylethyl amine (1.2 mmol, 174 VL), iodobenzene (1 mmol, 112
μL, 204 mg), butylacrylate (1.2 mmol, 173 μL). The reaction mixture was
stirred at 80°C (becomes orange during the reaction) for the desired time
and the organic phase extracted with diethyl ether (6 x 4 mL). The
organic containing methyl benzoate as internal standard (35 mg) was
analyzed GC and GC-MS. Evaporation of the volatiles affords yellow oil
that is mainly constituted of n-butyl trans-cinnamate as determined by 1H
and 13C NMR. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.68 (d, J = 15.9 Hz, 1H, CH
olefinic), 7.60-7.35(m, 5H, CH aromatic), 6.44 (d, J = 16 Hz, CH
olefinic), 1.46 (m, 2H, CH2), 1.70 (m, 2H, CH2), 4.21 (t, 2H, CH2), 0.96
(t, 3H, Me). 13C{1H} NMR (CDCl3): δ 167.1 (CO), 144.5, 134.4, 130.1,
128.8, 128.0, 118.3 (C aromatic and CH olefinic), 64.4 (CH2), 30.8 (CH2),
19.2 (CH2), 13.7 (Me). IR (neat, cm-1) 3061, 3030 (ν CH aromatic), 1713
(ν C=O), 1638 (ν C=C). GC-MS (m/z (%), EI, 70 eV): 131 (100, M+ -OBu),
103 (58), 51(54), 204 (10, M +), 77 (44).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM yield depends on reaction conditions, Heck Reaction, ionic liquid
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
