$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Stille Coupling:
Preparation of Trifluoromethanesulfonic Acid
2-[Benzyl-(4-methoxy-2-phenylbut-2-enoyl)-amino]phenyl Ester (10). A
stirred mixture of Pd2dba3·CHCl3 (6 mg, 0.006 mmol), P(2-furyl)3 (12 mg,
0.051 mmol), and freshly distilled N-methylpyyrolidinone (NMP, 2 mL) was
deoxygenated by bubbling Ar through a submerged needle for 1 h, during
which time a bright yellow solution resulted. A deoxygenated solution of
stannane 9 (200 mg, 0.28 mmol), iodobenzene (52 mg, 0.25 mmol), and NMP
(5 mL) was then added via syringe. Copper(I) iodide (46 mg, 0.28 mmol)
was then added, and the resulting mixture was flushed with a stream of Ar
for 15 min and then maintained at room temperature for 24 h. After
diluting the reaction with EtOAc (100 mL), the resulting solution was
washed with 5% aqueous NH4OH (3 × 10 mL) and brine (3 × 10 mL). The
organic layer was dried (Na2SO4) and filtered, and the filtrate was
concentrated. The residue was purified by flash chromatography (1:9-3:7
EtOAc-hexanes). Trifluoromethanesulfonic acid
2-[benzyl-(4-methoxy-2-pyridin-3-yl-but-2-enoyl)amino]phenyl ester (11b).
The general procedure for the Stille coupling was followed using stannane
9 (1.27 g, 1.76 mmol), 3-iodopyridine (392 mg, 1.94 mmol), Pd2dba3·CHCl3
(36 mg, 35 μmol, 2.0 mol%), P(2-furyl)3 (81 mg, 350 μmol, 0.2 equiv), and
CuI (371 mg, 1.94 mmol, 1.1 equiv). Silica gel column chromatography
(hexanes-ethyl acetate, 4:1-1:1, v/v) of the crude residue gave 11b (775
mg, 1.53 mmol, 87%, 10:1 mixture of amide rotamers) as a clear,
colorless, viscous oil. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3, major rotamer) δ 8.33
(dd, J = 4.5, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 7.94 (d, J = 2.0 Hz, 1H), 7.34-7.03 (m, 8H),
6.99 (dd, J = 7.5, 5.0 Hz, 1H), 6.84 (ddd, J = 7.5, 7.5, 1.0 Hz, 1H),
6.31 (dd, J = 8.0, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 5.89 (d, J = 14.0 Hz, 1H), 5.82 (t, J =
6.0 Hz, 1H), 4.19 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 2H), 3.94 (d, J = 14.0 Hz, 1H), 3.34
(s, 3H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 167.9, 148.9, 146.9, 145.6, 136.8,
136.4, 133.9, 133.5, 133.1, 133.0, 132.5, 130.2, 129.6, 128.8, 128.2,
128.0, 123.0, 121.6, 118.5 (q, J C,F = 319 Hz), 70.1, 58.6, 52.2; IR
(neat) 3034, 2930, 2826, 1660, 1494, 1420, 1247 cm-1; HRMS (CI) calcd for
C24H21F3N2O5S: 506.1123; found: 506.1129. Anal. Calcd for C24H21F3N2O5S:
C, 56.91; H, 4.18; N, 5.53. Found: C, 57.10; H, 4.34; N, 5.46.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM anaerobic, stereoselective, Stille coupling reaction, 10:1 mixt. of amide
rotamers
