$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure. The synthesis of 1 is given
as reference. In a 35 mL pressure tube, triethoxyvinylsilane (1.17 mL,
5.38 mmol) was added to an aqueous sodium hydroxide 0.50 M solution (13.5
mL, 6.75 mmol) containing a 20% (w/w) of PEG 2000 (2.7 g). The mixture
was vigorously stirred for 5 min at room temperature and
1-(4-bromophenyl)ethanone (0.2742 g, 1.35 mmol) and palladium(II) acetate
(0.3 mg, 1.4 μmol) were subsequently added. The tube was subsequently
introduced into a silicone bath, previously warmed to 140 °C, and
vigorously stirred for 3 h. Once this time elapsed, the reaction mixture
was allowed to cool to room temperature and extracted with ethyl acetate
(3 × 20 mL). The combined organic layers were dried over MgSO4 and, after
filtration, the solvent eliminated in a rotary evaporator connected to a
water aspirator pump. The purification was performed by column
chromatography on silica gel using a mixture of hexane/ethyl acetate as
eluent. 5-Vinyl-2-furanic acid (3). Following the general procedure,
triethoxyvinylsilane (1.30 mL, 5.98 mmol), an aqueous sodium hydroxide
solution 0.50 M (18.0 mL, 9.00 mmol), 5-bromo-2-furanic acid (0.2894 g,
1.50 mmol) and palladium(II) acetate (1.0 mg, 4.5 μmol) were warmed for 3
h at 140 °C. At the end of the reaction, the solution was acidified by
dropwise addition of hydrochloric acid 3 M. The product was obtained as a
white solid (0.1802 g, 87%) after extraction with diethyl ether and
purification by flash chromatography on silica gel with ethyl
acetate/ethanol 60:1 as eluent. (R f = 0.32). M. p.: 95-96 °C. 1H NMR
(CDCl3, 300 MHz): δ 5.41 (dd, 3 J c,a= 11.4, 3 J c,b= 0.9, 1 H; Hc),5.95
(dd, 3 J b,a= 17.6, 3 J b,c = 0.9, 1 H; Hb),6.40 (d, 3 J 4,3= 3.5, 1 H;
H4), 6.76 (dd, 3 J a,b= 17.6, 3 J a,c= 11.0,1 H; Ha), 7.28 (d, 3 J 3,4=
3.5, 1 H; H3). 13C{1H} NMR (CDCl3): δ 109.7 (C4), 117.7, 121.7, 124.3
(C3, CH, CH2), 142.5 (C2), 157.6 (C5), 163.5 (COOH). EI-MS (70 eV): m/z
(%) 138 (100) [M+], 121 (28) [M+ -OH], 93 (17) [M+ -COOH], 65 (67). IR
(KBr): ν 3340-2000 br, 2053 w, 1809 w, 1668 s, 1572 m, 1506 s, 1426 s,
1369 w, 1314 s, 1248 s, 1214 s, 1163 s, 1024 s, 981 m, 960 m, 900 s, 813
s, 760 s, 730 w, 680 w.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, thermal, Heck reaction, sealed tube used, product depends
on stoichiometry
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Mechanistic Studies on the Pd-Catalyzed Vinylation of Aryl Halides with
Vinylalkoxysilanes in Water: The Effect of the Solvent and NaOH Promoter
