$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The Heck reaction of aryl bromides with
styrene in the presence of catalysts 5a and 5b (Table 1). General
Procedure: An oven-dried Schlenk flask was charged under argon with
bromobenzene (527 μL, 784 mg 5.0 mmol), styrene (690 μL, 648 mg, 6.0
mmol), anhydrous KOAc (589 mg, 6.0 mmol) and DMA (5.0 mL). A solution of
catalyst 5a in DMA (4.48 x 10-4 M, 90 μL, 8.0 x 10-4 mol %) was then
added via syringe. The flask was sealed and placed in a 140 oC oil bath
controlled by a J-KEMP temperature controller and stirred for 24 h. After
cooling to rt, the reaction mixture was poured into water (200 mL) and
extracted with EtOAc (3 x 50 mL). The combined organic extracts were
washed with brine, dried with anhydrous Na2SO4, and concentrated.
Purification by flash chromatography on silica gel (hexanes/CH2Cl2 1:1)
gave trans-stilbene along with a trace amount of its regioisomer (790 mg,
87%). In another parallel run under identical conditions, the reaction
gave 778 mg (86%) of the products after workup and purification.
4-Methoxy-trans-stilbene2-41H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.54 (d, 2 H, d, J
= 7.8 Hz), 7.50 (d, 2 H, J = 8.7 Hz), 7.39 (t, 2 H, J = 7.6 Hz), 7.28 (t,
1 H, J = 7.3 Hz), 7.12 (d, 1 H, J = 16.3 Hz), 7.02 (d, 1 H, J = 16.3 Hz),
6.95 (d, 2 H, J = 8.7 Hz), 3.87 (s, 3 H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ
159.37, 137.71, 130.21, 128.67, 128.21, 127.75, 127.23, 126.68, 126.29,
114.19, 55.34.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective, Heck reaction, other product also
detected
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Carbocyclic Carbene Ligands Derived from Aromatic Nitrones: Formation and
Catalytic Activity of Their Pd(II) Complexes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Yao, Qingwei; Zabawa, Mark; Woo, Joyce; Zheng, Chong
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2007), 129(11), 3088-3089

