$DATUM (E)-2-(Diisopropyl(4-styrylphenyl)silyl)pyrimidine 1k: Was prepared via
Heck reaction of 1n with styrene.5 An oven dried 1 mL Wheaton V-vial
containing a stirring bar was charged with PyrDipSiAr 1n (70 mg, 0.2
mmol), Pd2(dba)3 (4.6 mg, 0.005 mmol), P(o-Tol)3 (6 mg, 0.02 mmol), K2CO3
(82.8 mg, 0.6 mmol), and TBAB (40 mg, 0.4 mmol) under N2 atmosphere
(glovebox). Dry DMF (0.2 mL) was added and the reaction vessel was capped
with a pressure screw cap. The reaction mixture was heated at 80 °C for
12 h. The resulting mixture was cooled down to room temperature, filtered
(Celite®, EtOAc), and concentrated under a reduced pressure. The residue
was purified by column chromatography on a silica gel (hexanes:EtOAc 8:1)
affording the corresponding product 1k in 92% yield. Yield 86%, colorless
oil. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ ppm 8.82 (d, J = 4.8 Hz, 2 H), 7.64 (d, J
= 7.7 Hz, 2 H), 7.52-7.53 (d, J = 4.8 Hz, 4 H), 7.36 (t, J = 7.7 Hz, 2
H), 7.22-7.24 (m, 2 H), 7.13 (AB system, J = 16.5, 5.5 Hz, 2 H), 1.71
