$DATUM A mixture of 26e (0.297 g, 0.69 mmol), PdCl2 (12.2 mg, 0.069 mmol, 10
mol%), PPh3 (36.2 mg, 0.138 mmol, 20 mol%), Cs2CO3 (0.562 g, 1.73 mmol,
2.5 eq), norbornene (0.389 g, 4.14 mmol, 6.0 eq), 8a (0.836 g, 4.14 mmol,
6.0 eq) in 1,4-dioxane (7.0 ml) in a schlenk tube was stirred at 85°C for
20 h. After being cooled to room temperature the mixture was filtered
through a plug of Celite eluting with ethyl acetate (20 ml). The filtrate
was washed with brine (15 ml), dried over sodium sulfate, and
concentrated. The crude product was purified by column chromatography
(10% ethyl acetate/ hexanes and 50% dichloromethane/ hexanes). 27e (0.249
g, 85%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.46 (s, 1 H), 7.82 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1
H), 7.64-7.37 (m, 3 H), 6.79 (s, 1 H), 5.80 (q, J = 9.2 Hz, 1 H), 5.15
(bs, 1 H), 4.76 (bs, 1 H), 4.72 (d, J = 17.2 Hz, 1 H), 4.19-4.00 (m, 1
H), 2.21-1.99 (m, 3 H), 1.99-1.83 (m, 2 H), 1.83-1.73 (m, 1 H), 1.73-1.60
(m, 2 H), 1.33 (s, 9 H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 179.0, 172.3, 150.0,
139.3, 133.6, 131.5, 130.8, 130.6, 128.4, 125.8, 124.1, 118.3, 115.4,
