$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for Synthesis of Indanones (II). To an oven-dried, 2-5
mL Biotage microwave vial with microstirrer is added carbonyl-ene product
(0.08 mmol, 1 equiv), 1,2,2,6,6-pentamethylpiperidine (2 equiv) and
PdCl2(PPh3)2 (1 mol%). The vial is capped with a crimp-cap and heated to
150 °C for 20-25 minutes in a Biotage microwave reactor. The reaction is
diluted with an equal volume of diethyl ether and poured into a
separatory funnel. The ethereal layer is washed with a saturated aqueous
NH4Cl solution (2 x 2 mL). The aqueous washes are back extracted with
diethyl ether (1 X 4 mL). The organic fractions are combined and washed
with brine (1 x 2 mL), dried with anhydrous MgSO4, filtered and
concentrated in vacuo. The crude products are purified via column
chromatography on silica gel.
(2S,3S)-2-ethanoyl-3-phenyl-2,3-dihydro-1H-inden-1-one (3) Compound 3 was
prepared according to the general procedure (II) using
(2a)-(R,Z)-3-((2-bromophenyl)(hydroxy)methyl)-4- phenylbut-3-en-2-one6
(25 mg, 0.075 mmol), PdCl2(PPh3)2 (~0.5 mg, 1 mol%) and 1,2,2,6,6-
pentamethylpiperidine (24 μL, 0.15 mmol) in DMF (1.0 mL). The crude
material was purified by column chromatography (15% Ethyl
Acetate:hexanes) to give the title compound as a white solid (15 mg,
85%). 91% ee by HPLC using Chiralcel OJ, 1 mL/min, 3-5% 2-propanol in
hexane tR = 7.54 (minor) and 10.74 (major) min (UV 254 nm). [α]D25 =
+198° (C = 0.56, CHCl3). FTIR (film) 3059, 3027, 2927, 1650, 1603, 1493,
1467, 1453, 1382, 1348, 1321, 1288, 1237, 894, 756, 739 cm-1. 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3) δ 14.10 (bs, 1H), 7.84 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 7.47 (ddd, J =
7.5, 7.5, 1.0 Hz, 1H), 7.39 (ddd, J = 7.5, 7.5, 0 Hz, 1H), 7.31-7.22 (bm,
5H), 7.16 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 2H), 4.85 (s, 1H), 1.83 (s, 3H) ppm. (500 MHz,
CDCl3) 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 193.2, 178.0, 152.8, 141.1, 136.7,
133.6, 128.9(2C), 127.7(2C), 127.7, 127.1, 125.6, 123.1, 115.7, 48.1,
20.8 ppm. MS (ESI) m/z calcd for [M]+ (C17H14O2H)+: 251 Found: [M+H]+
251.
