$DATUM Non-migration reaction conditions (procedure B): The appropriate aryl
iodide (0.25 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (2.8 mg, 0.0125 mmol), n-Bu4NCl (0.0694 g,
0.25 mmol), Et3N (50.5mg, 0.5 mmol) and ethyl acrylate (0.10 g, 1.0 mmol)
in DMF (1 ml) under Ar at 100 °C were stirred for the specified length of
time. The reaction mixture was then cooled to room temperature, diluted
with diethyl ether (35 mL) and washed with brine (30 mL). The aqueous
layer was reextracted with diethyl ether (15 mL). The organic layers were
combined, dried (MgSO4), filtered, and the solvent removed under reduced
pressure. The residue was purified by column chromatography on a silica
gel column. Ethyl E-3-(4'-nitrobiphen-2-yl)acrylate (2e). Compound 1e
(81.2 mg, 0.25 mmol) was allowed to react with ethyl acrylate under
non-migration reaction conditions (procedure B). After 1 d, the reaction
mixture was chromatographed using 5:1 hexanes/ethyl acetate toafford 63.1
mg (85%) of the indicated compound 2e as a yellow oil: 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ
1.29 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H), 4.22 (q, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 6.43 (d, J = 16.0 Hz,
1H), 7.36-7.38 (m, 1H), 7.46-7.51 (m, 4H), 7.60 (d, J = 15.6 Hz, 1H),
7.72-7.74 (m, 1H), 8.29-8.32 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 14.3, 60.7,
120.5, 123.6, 127.3, 129.0, 130.1, 130.3, 130.7, 132.7, 140.3, 142.4,
146.7, 147.3, 166.6; IR (CH2Cl2) 2917, 1710, 1517, 1348, 1314, 1179 cm-1;
HRMS m/z 297.1010 (calcd for C17H15NO4, 297.1001).
