$DATUM Stille Coupling to Prepare 8 and Deprotection to Form Enoate 9. A
suspension of Pd2(dba)3·CHCl3 (145 mg, 0.280 mmol Pd0), (2-furyl)3P (265
mg, 1.14 mmol), and dry NMP (8 mL) in a base-washed, flame-dried 100 mL
Schlenk flask was stirred for 2 h to furnish a yellow-green homogenous
solution. A solution of stannane 5 (1.70 g, 2.96 mmol), iodide 7 (1.04 g,
1.87 mmol), and NMP (12 mL) was added, and the reaction was degassed by
the freeze-pump-thaw method at -78 °C three times. Copper(I) iodide (620
mg, 3.26 mmol) was added, the mixture was stirred for 19 h at rt, and the
reaction was quenched by slow addition of saturated aqueous KF (10 mL).
After stirring for 15 min, the mixture was diluted with MTBE (400 mL) and
washed with water (300 mL) containing concentrated ammonia solution (15
mL). The aqueous layer was extracted with MTBE (200 mL). The combined
organic extracts were dried (MgSO4), filtered, concentrated, and the
residue was purified by silica gel chromatography (13:1, 9:1, 6:1, 4:1
hexanes-ethyl acetate) to give 1.19 g of 8 as a colorless foam. A
solution of 8 (1.19 g) and DMSO (25 mL) was degassed[bubbling argon (30
min), evacuate (15 min, 5 mm), bubbling argon (30 min)] and then heated
at 130°C for 6.5 h. The reaction was poured into water (200 mL) and
extracted with Et2O (50 mL × 3). The combined organic extracts were dried
(MgSO4), filtered, concentrated, and the residue was purified by silica
gel chromatography (8:1, 6:1, 5:1 hexanes-ethyl acetate) to give 939 mg
(82%) of 9 as a colorless foam. MS (ESI) m/z 736.43 (736.38 calcd for
C38H55N3NaO 10 , M+Na). :[α]24D = -41.7,[α]24577 = -43.9,[α]24546 =
-52.6,[α]24435 = -126,[α]24405 = -166 (c 0.79, CHCl3); 1H NMR (500 MHz,
DMSO, 80 °C) δ 10.23 (s, 1H, NH), 7.61 (br d,J= 7.7 Hz, 1H, ArH), 7.13
(d,J= 2.3 Hz, 1H, ArH), 7.01 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H, ArH), 6.92 (dd, J = 7.2,
0.8 Hz, 1H, ArH), 6.28 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H, C═CH), 5.16 (app td, J = 7.4,
4.3 Hz, 1H, CHN), 4.29 (dd, J = 9.0, 7.0 Hz, 1H, CH2O), 4.14-4.10 (m, 1H,
CHN), 3.98 (br, 1H, CH2O), 3.80 (dd, J = 7.9, 5.8 Hz, 1H, CH2O), 3.74
(dd, J = 8.8, 1.6 Hz, 1H, CH2O), 3.68 (s, 3H, CO2Me), 3.15 (dd, J = 13.8,
2.8 Hz, 1H, CH2), 2.81 (dd, J = 13.8, 10.2 Hz, 1H, CH2), 1.53 (s, 6H,
Me2C), 1.50 (s, 3H, MeCMe), 1.48 (s, 9H, t-Bu), 1.44 (s, 9H, t-Bu), 1.43
(s, 3H, MeCMe); 13C NMR (125 MHz, DMSO, 80°C) δ 165.8, 151.2, 151.0,
146.7, 134.0, 130.2, 127.5, 123.4, 121.7, 121.3, 118.0.
