$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 23. Using a modification of procedures
reported by Denmark,17 in a nitrogen filled glovebox, a 4 mL vial
equipped with a stirbar and a Teflon lined septum cap was charged with
tetrabutylammnium fluoride trihydrate (315 mg, 1 mmol). The sealed vial
was brought out of the glovebox and was connected to nitrogen via a
double manifold. Toluene (700 μL) was added to the vial via syringe with
stirring followed by H2O (90 μL, 5 mmol), which was added via syringe to
form a solution of tetrabutylammonium fluoride octahydrate. A hot 15 mL
high pressure reaction vessel equipped with a stir bar and a Teflon valve
was attached to a double manifold and was allowed to cool to room
temperature under vacuum. The vessel was backfilled with nitrogen, opened
to air, and 2-dicyclohexylphosphino-2’-4’-6’-triisopropylbiphenyl (XPhos,
53 mg, 0.11 mmol) and Pd(dba)2 (29 mg, 0.05 mmol) were added. The Teflon
valve was then replaced, and the vessel was evacuated and backfilled with
nitrogen three times. Next, under positive nitrogen pressure, the cap was
then replaced with a septum. The solution of tetrabutylammonium fluoride
octahydrate was transferred to the high pressure reaction vessel via
syringe, with stirring, and the vial was rinsed with toluene (300 μL)
which was also added to the high pressure reaction vessel via syringe.
The mixture was stirred for 25 minutes before the silane (5a: 118 mg or
5b: 125 mg, 0.5mmol) and phenyl trifluoromethanesulfonate (120 μL, 0.75
mmol) were sequentially added, each in one portion, via syringe with
stirring. The Teflon valve was replaced under positive nitrogen pressure,
and the reaction vessel was sealed. The vessel was then heated at 90 ºC
in an oil bath with stirring for 16 h, after which time the reaction was
cooled to rt. The reaction vessel was then opened to air, and
approximately 5 mL of brine and 10 mL of diethyl ether were added. The
organic layer was removed, and the brine was extracted twice more with 10
mL portions of diethyl ether. The combined organic layers were dried
(MgSO4), filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The product was purified
using flash silica chromatography (0-10% CH2Cl2:hexanes) and concentrated
in vacuo. 88 mg (84%, from 5b) of a white solid. Product 23.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
