$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure. The synthesis of 18 is
given as reference. In a 35 mL pressure tube, triethoxyvinylsilane (0.77
mL, 3.5 mmol) was added to an aqueous sodium hydroxide 0.50 M solution
(10.7 mL, 5.35 mmol) containing a 20% (w/w) of PEG 2000 (2.14 g). The
mixture was vigorously stirred for 5 min at room temperature and
3-bromopyridine (0.178 mL, 1.78 mmol) and palladium(II) acetate (0.4 mg,
1.8 μmol) were subsequently added. The reaction mixture was vigorously
stirred for 3 h at 140 °C. Then, 1-(4-bromophenyl)ethanone (0.3615 g,
1.80 mmol) and palladium(II) acetate (0.4 mg, 1.8 μmol) were added and
the reaction mixture was again stirred for 6 h at 140 °C. When the
reaction time elapsed, the mixture was worked up as described above.
(E)-5-(2-(Pyridin-3-yl)ethenyl)furan-2-carboxylic acid (19). Following
the general procedure, triethoxyvinylsilane (0.77 mL, 3.5 mmol), an
aqueous sodium hydroxide solution 0.50 M (15.0 mL, 7.5 mmol), PEG 2000
(3.0 g) and (A) 3-bromopyridine (0.178 mL, 1.78 mmol) and palladium(II)
acetate (0.4 mg, 1.8 μmol) were warmed for 3 h at 140 °C. Subsequently
(B), 5-bromo-2-furancarboxylic acid (0.3434 g, 1.78 mmol) and
palladium(II) acetate (0.4 mg, 1.8 μmol) were added and the mixture
warmed for other 6 h at 140 °C. The solution was filtered and
subsequently acidified by dropwise addition of hydrochloric acid 3 M.
Then, the solution was filtered to remove the insoluble
(E)-1,2-bis-[5-carboxyfuranyl]ethene and the resulting solution was
neutralised with NaOH (0.5 M). The precipitate was filtered. The product
as a yellow-green solid (0.3219 g, 84%). M. p.: ≈ 250 °C (dec.). 1H NMR
(DMSO-d6 , 500 MHz): δ 6.75 (d, 3 J 10,11 = 3.6, 1 H; H10), 7.21 (d, 3 J
7,8 = 16.3, 1 H; H7), 7.25 (d, 3 J 11,10= 3.6, 1 H; H11), 7.33 (d, 3 J
8,7 = 16.6, 1 H; H8), 7.40 (dd, 3 J 5,4= 7.8, 3 J 5,6= 4.8, 1 H; H5),
8.06 (d, 3 J 4,5= 8.0, 1 H; H4), 8.47 (d, 3 J 6,5= 3.9, 1 H; H6), 8.79
(s, 1 H; H2). 13C{1H} NMR (DMSO-d6 , 125 MHz): δ 110.9 (C10), 117.4 (C8),
119.1 (C11), 123.3 (C5), 126.1 (C7), 131.3 (C3), 132.5 (C4), 143.8 (C12),
148.1 (C2), 148.5 (C6), 155.0 (C9), 158.7 (COOH). ESI-TOF HRMS: m/z
216.0661 [M + H]+. Calcd for C12H9NO3·H+: 216.0674. IR (KBr): ν 3700-2200
br, 1701 s, 1640 m, 1507 s, 1386 m, 1361 m, 1287 m, 1148 s, 960 s, 808 m,
780 m, 702 w, 683 w, 647 w, 623 w.
