$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the 1,4-palladium alkyl
to aryl migration. A mixture of aryl halide (0.25 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (2.8
mg, 0.0125 mmol), bis(diphenylphosphino)methane (4.8 mg, 0.0125 mmol),
cesium pivalate (0.1170 g, 0.5 mmol), and the indicated amounts of alkene
(if employed) in dry DMF (4 mL) was quickly flushed with argon and
stirred at the indicated reaction temperature. The reaction was monitored
by TLC and gas chromatographic analysis. After the reaction was complete,
it was diluted with ethyl ether, washed with satd aq NaHCO3, dried over
Na2SO4, concentrated, and purified by flash chromatography on silica gel.
12b-Methyl-1,12b-dihydro-2H-benzo[5,6]indeno[1,2,3-de]chromene (8). The
reaction mixture was chromatographed using 30:1 hexane/EtOAc to afford 57
mg of the indicated compound (84 % yield) as a white solid: mp 154-156
°C; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 1.52 (s, 3H), 1.76-1.87 (m, 1H), 2.41 (dd, J = 3.6,
12.9 Hz, 1H), 4.59 (dd, J = 6.0, 11.4 Hz, 1H), 4.63-4.73 (m, 1H), 6.76
(d, J = 11.1 Hz, 1H), 7.25-7.30 (m, 1H), 7.37 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H),
7.45-7.48 (m, 2H), 7.81 (s, 1H), 7.81-7.85 (m, 1H), 7.88-7.91 (m, 1H),
8.11 (s, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 26.9, 31.5, 42.1, 65.6, 113.1, 114.3,
119.5, 121.6, 125.9, 125.9, 128.1, 128.5, 129.7, 133.1, 133.6, 135.4,
139.1, 140.0, 151.9, 153.0; IR (CHCl3, cm-1) 3017, 2965, 1614, 1591,
1484; HRMS Calcd for C20H16O: 272.1201. Found: 272.1208.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
