$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Synthesis of Indanones
(II). To an oven-dried, 2-5 mL Biotage microwave vial with microstirrer
is added carbonyl-ene product (0.08 mmol, 1 equiv),
1,2,2,6,6-pentamethylpiperidine (2 equiv) and PdCl2(PPh3)2 (1 mol%). The
vial is capped with a crimp-cap and heated to 150 °C for 20-25 minutes in
a Biotage microwave reactor. The reaction is diluted with an equal volume
of diethyl ether and poured into a separatory funnel. The ethereal layer
is washed with a saturated aqueous NH4Cl solution (2 x 2 mL). The aqueous
washes are back extracted with diethyl ether (1 X 4 mL). The organic
fractions are combined and washed with brine (1 x 2 mL), dried with
anhydrous MgSO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo. The crude products
are purified via column chromatography on silica gel.
(2S,3S)-2-hexanoyl-3-phenyl-2,3-dihydro-1H-inden-1-one (6g) Compound 6g
was prepared according to the general procedure (II) using
(R,Z)-2-((2-bromophenyl)(hydroxy)methyl)-1- phenyloct-1-en-3-one (30 mg,
0.077 mmol), PdCl2(PPh3)2 (~0.5 mg, 1 mol%) and
1,2,2,6,6-pentamethylpiperidine (27 μL, 0.154 mmol) in DMF (1.0 mL). The
crude material was purified by column chromatography (15% Ethyl
Acetate:hexanes) to give the title compound as a white solid (20 mg,
84%). 86% ee by HPLC using Chiralcel OJ, 0.5 mL/min, 2% 2-propanol in
hexane tR = 8.12 (minor) and 10.04 (major) min (UV 254 nm). FTIR (film)
3062, 3027, 2957, 2929, 2860, 1646, 1609, 1466, 1377, 1324, 1237, 742,
701 cm-1. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 14.22 (s, 1H), 7.84 (ddd, J = 7.6,
0.9, 0.9 Hz, 1H), 7.47 (ddd, J = 7.5, 7.5, 1.1 Hz, 1H), 7.39 (dd, J =
7.4, 7.4 Hz, 1H), 7.31-7.26 (bm, 3H), 7.24-7.20 (bm, 2H), 7.14 (m, 2H),
4.85 (s, 1H), 2.12 (ddd, J = 14.1, 9.0, 6.5 Hz, 1H), 2.04 (ddd, J = 14.1,
8.9, 6.0 Hz, 2H), 1.48 (dddd, J = 6.5, 7, 4.5, 2 Hz, 1H), 1.31-1.22 (bm,
2H), 1.19-1.11 (bm, 2H), 1.10-1.03 (bm, 2H), 0.78 (t, 3H) ppm. 13C NMR
(125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 193.6, 181.3, 152.8, 141.5, 136.9, 133.5, 128.8(2C),
127.8(2C), 127.7, 127.0, 125.9, 123.0, 115.6, 48.0, 34.1, 31.4, 25.1,
22.3, 13.8 ppm. MS (ESI) m/z calcd for [M+H]+ (C21H22O2)+: 306 Found:
[M]+ 306.
