$DATUM 75-09-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1-iodo-2-(2-methylenebutyl)benzene (11): A
magnetic stir bar, precatalyst 1 (0.050 mmol, 36.7 mg), 2-iodobenzyl
chloride (1.00 mmol, 252 mg), Et3N (6.00 mmol, 836 μL), and
dichloromethane (500 μL) were added to an 8 mL screw-cap vial, which was
fitted with a rubber septum. A stream of 1- butene gas was bubbled
through the solution for 10 minutes to saturate the solution, after which
the reaction was kept under a static atmosphere of 1-butene with a
balloon. Trimethylsilyl triflate (1.50 mmol, 271 μL) was added via
syringe and the reaction mixture was allowed to stir for 6 hours.
Following work-up according to the general procedure, silica gel
chromatography yielded 10. After the necessary time had elapsed, the
reaction mixture was allowed to stir open to the air for 5 minutes, after
which it was passed through a 4 cm plug of silica gel (pre-wetted with
dichloromethane). The silica gel plug was washed with 25 mL of
dichloromethane followed by 25 mL of a 1:1 mixture of hexanes/ethyl
acetate. After concentration under reduced pressure, the crude material
was purified by column chromatography on silica gel with the indicated
eluent. Clear, colorless liquid, yield (229 mg, 84%, 95:5 ratio). Rf =
0.64. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.86 (dd, J = 7.9, 1.3 Hz, 1H), 7.31 (td,
J = 7.5, 1.3 Hz, 1H), 7.24 (ddd, J = 7.6, 1.7, 0.4 Hz, 1H), 6.93 (td, J =
7.8, 1.8 Hz, 1H), 4.93 (qd, J = 1.5, 0.7 Hz, 1H), 4.57 (qt, J = 1.5, 0.9
Hz, 1H), 3.50 (s, 1H), 2.12 (qdd, J = 7.4, 1.6, 0.8 Hz, 2H), 1.13 (t, J =
7.4 Hz, 3H). 13C{1H} NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3) δ 149.23, 142.73, 139.55,
130.23, 128.24, 127.96, 110.58, 101.75, 47.49, 29.12, 12.47. IR (ATR,
cm-1): 3061 (w), 2965 (w), 2934 (w), 2878 (w), 1647 (w), 1585 (w), 1561
(w), 1464 (m), 1434 (m), 1374 (w), 1046 (w), 1011 (s), 891 (s), 742 (s),
714 (m). HRMS (DART, m/z): [M + H]+ calcd for C11H13I, 273.0135; found,
273.0132.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, catalyst prepared and used, Mizoroki-Heck-type reaction,
other products also detected, gaseous 1-butene used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Simplifying Nickel(0) Catalysis: An Air-Stable Nickel Precatalyst for the
Internally Selective Benzylation of Terminal Alkenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Standley, Eric A.; Jamison, Timothy F.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2013), 135(4), 1585-1592

