$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Heck Arylation of Olefins: An oven-dried
carousel reaction tube containing a stirrer bar was charged with aryl
chloride 1 (1.0 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (0.01 mmol), 4-MeOdppp (0.015 mmol), and
KOH (1.5 mmol). After degassing three times with nitrogen, ethylene
glycol (4 mL) and n-butyl vinyl ether 2a (3.0 mmol) were injected
sequentially. The reaction mixture was vigorously stirred at 145 °C for
10 h. After cooling down to room temperature, 2 mL aqueous HCl (3 M) and
10 mL Et2O were added; the mixture was stirred for 1 h. After separation
of the Et2O phase, the aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O (3 x 10 mL)
and the combined organic layers were washed with brine, dried over
Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo (When aqueous hydrolysis was
not necessary, the product was directly extracted from EG with Et2O). The
crude product was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel using a
mixture of ethyl acetate and hexane (5/95 to 50/50) as eluant.
Acetophenone (3a), yield 83%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.98-7.95 (m,
2H), 7.58-7.55 (m, 1H), 7.48-7.44 (m, 2H), 2.61 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3) δ 198.6, 137.5, 133.5, 129.0, 128.7, 27.0; MS (CI, m/z, %)
138 (100) [M+NH3+H]+; Anal. calcd for C8H8O: C, 79.97; H, 6.71. Found: C,
80.17; H, 6.78.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Heck reaction, mechanism studied, kinetics studied,
carousel reaction tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Hydrogen-Bonding-Promoted Oxidative Addition and Regioselective Arylation
of Olefins with Aryl Chlorides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ruan, Jiwu; Iggo, Jonathan A.; Berry, Neil G.; Xiao, Jianliang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2010), 132(46), 16689-16699

