$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Synthesis of Indanones
(II). To an oven-dried, 2-5 mL Biotage microwave vial with microstirrer
is added carbonyl-ene product (0.08 mmol, 1 equiv),
1,2,2,6,6-pentamethylpiperidine (2 equiv) and PdCl2(PPh3)2 (1 mol%). The
vial is capped with a crimp-cap and heated to 150 °C for 20-25 minutes in
a Biotage microwave reactor. The reaction is diluted with an equal volume
of diethyl ether and poured into a separatory funnel. The ethereal layer
is washed with a saturated aqueous NH4Cl solution (2 x 2 mL). The aqueous
washes are back extracted with diethyl ether (1 X 4 mL). The organic
fractions are combined and washed with brine (1 x 2 mL), dried with
anhydrous MgSO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo. The crude products
are purified via column chromatography on silica gel.
(2S,3S)-2-bromo-3-(3-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)propyl)-2-ethanoyl-2,3-dihydro-1H-inden-1-one
(6d-Br) Compound 6d was prepared according to the general procedure (II)
using (43 mg, 0.100 mmol), PdCl2(PPh3)2 (~0.5 mg, 1 mol%) and
1,2,2,6,6-pentamethylpiperidine (36 μL, 0.154 mmol) in DMF (1.0 mL). The
crude material was purified by column chromatography (15% Ethyl
Acetate:hexanes) to give the title compound as a mixture of enol
tautomers (29 mg, 83%) tR = 19.71 (major) and 21.75 (minor) min (UV 254
nm). FTIR (film) 2953, 2929, 2885, 1723, 1706, 1604, 1471, 1464, 1357,
1267, 1255, 1205, 1104, 836, 776 cm-1. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.77 (d,
J = 7.7 Hz, 1H), 7.7 (ddd, J = 7.5, 7.5, 1.0 Hz, 1H), 7.50 (dd, J = 7.9,
1.0 Hz, 1H), 7.43 (ddd, J = 7.5, 7.5, 0 Hz, 1H), 4.14 (dd, J = 8.8, 5.0
Hz, 1H), 3.70- 3.62 (m, 2H), 2.64 (s, 3H), 2.16-2.09 (m, 1H), 1.92-1.85
(m, 1H), 1.60-1.55 (m, 2H), 0.89 (s, 9H), 0.05 (s, 6H) ppm. 13C NMR (125
MHz, CDCl3) δ 200.2, 196.0, 154.1, 136.2, 131.6, 128.5, 125.3(2C), 74.4,
62.5, 44.4, 30.6, 29.6, 28.1, 25.9(3C), 18.2, -5.3(2C) ppm. MS (ESI) m/z
calcd for [M+Na]+ (C20H29BrO3SiNa)+: 447, 449 Found: [M+Na]+ 447, 449.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Enantioselective Synthesis of Substituted Indanones from Silyloxyallenes
