$DATUM (E)-N-tert-Butyl 4-iso-propyl penta-2,4-dienamide (entry 4). Lithium
chloride (169.6 mg, 4.00 mmol), X-Phos (9.6 mg, 0.02 mmol), 3-methyl
but-1-en-2-yl diphenylphosphate (191.0 mg, 0.60 mmol), N-tert- butyl
acrylamide (50.9 mg, 0.40 mmol), Cy2NMe (170μL, 0.80 mmol), PdCl2(COD)
(5.7 mg, 0.02 mmol) dissolved in a 1:1 DMFDioxane mixture (3 mL) were
reacted for 24 h at 100°C. The crude product was purified by flash
chromatography on silica gel using CH2Cl2 as eluent. This afforded 65 mg
of the title compound (83% yield) as a colorless solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CD3CN) δ (ppm) 7.07 (d, 1H, J = 15.4 Hz), 6.32 (bs, 1H, NH), 6.08 (d, 1H,
J = 15.4 Hz), 5.30 (s, 1H), 5.26 (s, 1H), 2.61 (septet, 1H, J = 6.8 Hz),
1.35 (s, 9H), 1.12 (d, 6H, J = 6.8 Hz). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CD3CN) 166.0,
152.7, 141.3, 123.3, 118.0, 51.6, 30.1, 28.9, 22.4. HRMS C12H21NO
[M+Na+]: 218.1521 found: 218.1526.
