$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure. The synthesis of 1 is given
as reference. In a 35 mL pressure tube, triethoxyvinylsilane (1.17 mL,
5.38 mmol) was added to an aqueous sodium hydroxide 0.50 M solution (13.5
mL, 6.75 mmol) containing a 20% (w/w) of PEG 2000 (2.7 g). The mixture
was vigorously stirred for 5 min at room temperature and
1-(4-bromophenyl)ethanone (0.2742 g, 1.35 mmol) and palladium(II) acetate
(0.3 mg, 1.4 μmol) were subsequently added. The tube was subsequently
introduced into a silicone bath, previously warmed to 140 °C, and
vigorously stirred for 3 h. Once this time elapsed, the reaction mixture
was allowed to cool to room temperature and extracted with ethyl acetate
(3 × 20 mL). The combined organic layers were dried over MgSO4 and, after
filtration, the solvent eliminated in a rotary evaporator connected to a
water aspirator pump. The purification was performed by column
chromatography on silica gel using a mixture of hexane/ethyl acetate as
eluent. (E)-1,2-Bis-[5-carboxyfuran-2-yl]ethene (12). Following the
general procedure, triethoxyvinylsilane (0.39 mL, 1.8 mmol), an aqueous
sodium hydroxide solution 0.50 M (18.0 mL, 9.00 mmol), 5-bromo-2-furanic
acid (0.5788 g, 3.00 mmol) and palladium(II) acetate (20.0 mg, 8.9 mmol)
were warmed for 5 h at 140 °C. The solution was cooled to room
temperature and filtered. Hydrochloric acid 3 M was then dropwise added
to reach an acid pH and the mixture was cooled for 5 min. The product was
separated by filtration, washed with warm ethanol, and isolated, A white
solid (0.0894 g, 83%). M. p.: 300 °C. Anal. Calcd for C12H8O6: C, 58.07;
H, 3.25. Found: C, 57.63; H, 3.26. 1H NMR (DMSO-d6 , 300 MHz): δ 6.85 (d,
3 J 4,3= 3.6, 2 H; H3), 7.25 (d, 3 J 3,4= 3.6, 2 H; H4), 7.07 (s, 2 H;
Ha), 13.10 (s, 2 H; COOH). 13C{1H} NMR (DMSO-d6 ): δ 112.0 (C4), 116.3
(C3), 119.2 (Ca), 143.9 (C2), 154.3 (C5), 158.5 (COOH). ESI-TOF HRMS: m/z
249.0388 [M + H]+. Calcd for C12H8O6·H+: 249.0399. IR (KBr): ν 3500-2300
br, 1686 s, 1578 w, 1522 s, 1420 m, 1309 m, 1257 m, 1193 m, 1153 m, 1022
m, 957 m, 807 m, 762 m.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, thermal, Heck reaction, sealed tube used, product depends
on stoichiometry
