$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The reaction of 8a and butyl acrylate (9b) was
found to proceed very efficiently with only 1 mol ppm of the pincer
catalyst 2c by employing an NMP/H2O mixture (7:3) as a solvent to give
90% isolated yield of butyl trans-cinnamate 11a. Compound 11b.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, thermal, Heck reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM NCN Pincer Palladium Complexes: Their Preparation via a Ligand
Introduction Route and Their Catalytic Properties
